From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: openEuler RISC-V Package Automation <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] libsent: restrict cpuid header to x86

calc_dnn.c includes GCC's x86-only cpuid.h on every non-Windows target
except ARM. RISC-V does not enable the x86 SIMD implementations and uses
the existing scalar DNN path, so limit the header to the architectures
that can use it.

Patch-Source: openEuler RISC-V package CI failure analysis
Patch-License: BSD-3-Clause
Upstream-Status: Not Submitted (automated upstream writes are not authorized)
Remove-When: Upstream restricts cpuid.h to x86 targets in a stable release.
---
 libsent/src/phmm/calc_dnn.c | 7 ++-----
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libsent/src/phmm/calc_dnn.c b/libsent/src/phmm/calc_dnn.c
--- a/libsent/src/phmm/calc_dnn.c
+++ b/libsent/src/phmm/calc_dnn.c
@@ -12,12 +12,9 @@
 #ifdef _WIN32
 #include <intrin.h>
-#else
-#if defined(__arm__) || TARGET_OS_IPHONE || defined(__aarch64__)
-#else
+#elif defined(__i386__) || defined(__x86_64__)
 #include <cpuid.h>
 #endif
-#endif	/* _WIN32 */
-
+
 #include <sent/stddefs.h>
 #include <sent/htk_hmm.h>
 #include <sent/htk_param.h>
--
2.50.1
